.\" kpm(1) - Kubernetes Pods Metrics
.TH KPM 1 "2026-10-11" "kpm v0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kpm \- Kubernetes Pods Metrics (sample CPU/mem, recommend rightsizing)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kpm
.I command
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kpm
is a Go CLI that samples pod CPU and memory metrics into a local
.B SQLite
store and surfaces rightsizing recommendations.
It uses
.B client-go
directly (no
.BR kubectl
binary) once the sampler is implemented.
.PP
Behavior contract:
.B SPECIFICATIONS.md
and roadmap
.BR docs/ROADMAP.md .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-print\-sample\-config
Print the embedded sample configuration to stdout and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B version
Print version and build metadata.
.TP
.B sample
Sample pod CPU/memory into SQLite
.RB ( \-\-config ,
.BR \-\-kubeconfig ).
.B sample.interval_seconds: 0
is one-shot;
.B > 0
runs a daemon loop until SIGINT/SIGTERM.
.TP
.B backup
Safe SQLite copy via
.B VACUUM INTO
.RB ( \-\-config ,
.BR \-o ).
.TP
.B export
Export samples as
.B csv
or
.B tsv
.RB ( \-\-format ,
.BR \-o ,
.BR \-\-since ,
.BR \-\-until ,
.BR \-\-namespace ,
.BR \-\-pod ,
.BR \-\-workload ).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kubectl-kpm (1),
.I https://github.com/hrodrig/kpm
.SH AUTHOR
Hermes Rodríguez and contributors.
